<http://rs.tdwg.org/ac/terms/endTimestamp> <http://rs.tdwg.org/dwc/terms/attributes/organizedInClass> <http://rs.tdwg.org/ac/terms/RegionOfInterest> .
<http://rs.tdwg.org/ac/terms/endTimestamp> <http://rs.tdwg.org/dwc/terms/attributes/repeatable> "No" .
<http://rs.tdwg.org/ac/terms/endTimestamp> <http://rs.tdwg.org/dwc/terms/attributes/required> "No" .
<http://rs.tdwg.org/ac/terms/endTimestamp> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#Property> .
<http://rs.tdwg.org/ac/terms/endTimestamp> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The end of a temporal region, specified as real-world clock time ISO 8601 timestamps, using UTC timezone, with an optional fractional part to indicate milliseconds or finer. There is no limit on the number of decimal places for the decimal fraction."@en .
<http://rs.tdwg.org/ac/terms/endTimestamp> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <http://rs.tdwg.org/ac/terms/> .
<http://rs.tdwg.org/ac/terms/endTimestamp> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "End Timestamp"@en .
<http://rs.tdwg.org/ac/terms/endTimestamp> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The end of a temporal region, specified as real-world clock time ISO 8601 timestamps, using UTC timezone, with an optional fractional part to indicate milliseconds or finer. There is no limit on the number of decimal places for the decimal fraction."@en .
<http://rs.tdwg.org/ac/terms/endTimestamp> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "End Timestamp"@en .
<http://rs.tdwg.org/ac/terms/endTimestamp> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "This term MAY be applied to a region of interest or an entire media item."@en .
