<http://rs.tdwg.org/ac/terms/metadataLanguageLiteral> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Language of description and other metadata (but not necessarily of the image itself) represented as an ISO639-2 three letter language code."@en .
<http://rs.tdwg.org/ac/terms/metadataLanguageLiteral> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Metadata Language"@en .
<http://rs.tdwg.org/ac/terms/metadataLanguageLiteral> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "ISO639-1 two-letter codes are permitted but deprecated. At least one of ac:metadataLanguage and ac:metadataLanguageLiteral MUST be supplied but, when feasible, supplying both might make the metadata more widely useful. They MUST specify the same language. In case of ambiguity, ac:metadataLanguage prevails."@en .
