<http://rs.tdwg.org/ac/terms/physicalSetting> <http://rs.tdwg.org/dwc/terms/attributes/organizedInClass> <http://rs.tdwg.org/dwc/terms/attributes/ContentCoverage> .
<http://rs.tdwg.org/ac/terms/physicalSetting> <http://rs.tdwg.org/dwc/terms/attributes/repeatable> "Yes" .
<http://rs.tdwg.org/ac/terms/physicalSetting> <http://rs.tdwg.org/dwc/terms/attributes/required> "No" .
<http://rs.tdwg.org/ac/terms/physicalSetting> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#Property> .
<http://rs.tdwg.org/ac/terms/physicalSetting> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The setting of the content represented in media such as images, sounds, and movies if the provider deems them relevant."@en .
<http://rs.tdwg.org/ac/terms/physicalSetting> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <http://rs.tdwg.org/ac/terms/> .
<http://rs.tdwg.org/ac/terms/physicalSetting> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Physical Setting"@en .
<http://rs.tdwg.org/ac/terms/physicalSetting> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The setting of the content represented in media such as images, sounds, and movies if the provider deems them relevant."@en .
<http://rs.tdwg.org/ac/terms/physicalSetting> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Physical Setting"@en .
<http://rs.tdwg.org/ac/terms/physicalSetting> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Constrained vocabulary of: \"Natural\" = Object in its natural setting of the object (e.g., living organisms in their natural environment); \"Artificial\" = Object in an artificial environment (e.g., living organisms in an artificial environment such as a zoo, garden, greenhouse, or laboratory); \"Edited\" = Human media editing of a natural setting or media acquisition with a separate media background such as a photographic backdrop."@en .
