<http://rs.tdwg.org/ac/terms/subtypeLiteral> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Subtype (literal)"@en .
<http://rs.tdwg.org/ac/terms/subtypeLiteral> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "The subtypeLiteral term MUST NOT be applied to Collection objects. However, the Description term in the Content Coverage Vocabulary might add further description to a Collection object. Controlled string values SHOULD be selected from the Controlled Vocabulary for Audiovisual Core subtype. Human-readable information about the Controlled Vocabulary for subtype is at http://rs.tdwg.org/ac/doc/subtype/ . It is best practice to use ac:subtype instead of ac:subytpeLiteral whenever practical."@en .
<http://rs.tdwg.org/ac/terms/tag.rdf> <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator> "Biodiversity Information Standards (TDWG)" .
<http://rs.tdwg.org/ac/terms/tag.rdf> <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/format> "application/rdf+xml" .
<http://rs.tdwg.org/ac/terms/tag.rdf> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/modified> "2020-01-27T08:59:43-06:00"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> .
<http://rs.tdwg.org/ac/terms/tag.rdf> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/references> <http://rs.tdwg.org/ac/terms/tag> .
<http://rs.tdwg.org/ac/terms/tag.rdf> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/document> .
<http://rs.tdwg.org/ac/terms/tag> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "2013-10-28"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
<http://rs.tdwg.org/ac/terms/tag> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "Tags may be multi-worded phrases. Where scientific names, common names, geographic locations, etc. are separable, those should go into the more specific coverage metadata items provided further below. Examples: \"flower diagram\". Character or part keywords like \"leaf\", or \"flower color\" are especially desirable."@en .
<http://rs.tdwg.org/ac/terms/tag> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/hasVersion> <http://rs.tdwg.org/ac/terms/version/tag-2013-10-28> .
