<http://rs.tdwg.org/ac/terms/widthFrac.rdf> <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator> "Biodiversity Information Standards (TDWG)" .
<http://rs.tdwg.org/ac/terms/widthFrac.rdf> <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/format> "application/rdf+xml" .
<http://rs.tdwg.org/ac/terms/widthFrac.rdf> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/modified> "2021-10-07T13:17:47-05:00"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> .
<http://rs.tdwg.org/ac/terms/widthFrac.rdf> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/references> <http://rs.tdwg.org/ac/terms/widthFrac> .
<http://rs.tdwg.org/ac/terms/widthFrac.rdf> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/document> .
<http://rs.tdwg.org/ac/terms/widthFrac> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "2021-10-05"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
<http://rs.tdwg.org/ac/terms/widthFrac> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "Zero-sized bounding rectangles are not allowed. To designate a point, use the radius option with a zero value."@en .
<http://rs.tdwg.org/ac/terms/widthFrac> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/hasVersion> <http://rs.tdwg.org/ac/terms/version/widthFrac-2021-10-05> .
<http://rs.tdwg.org/ac/terms/widthFrac> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/isPartOf> <http://rs.tdwg.org/ac/terms/> .
<http://rs.tdwg.org/ac/terms/widthFrac> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/modified> "2021-10-05"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
<http://rs.tdwg.org/ac/terms/widthFrac> <http://rs.tdwg.org/dwc/terms/attributes/organizedInClass> <http://rs.tdwg.org/ac/terms/RegionOfInterest> .
<http://rs.tdwg.org/ac/terms/widthFrac> <http://rs.tdwg.org/dwc/terms/attributes/repeatable> "No" .
<http://rs.tdwg.org/ac/terms/widthFrac> <http://rs.tdwg.org/dwc/terms/attributes/required> "No" .
<http://rs.tdwg.org/ac/terms/widthFrac> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#Property> .
<http://rs.tdwg.org/ac/terms/widthFrac> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The width of the bounding rectangle, expressed as a decimal fraction of the width of the media item."@en .
<http://rs.tdwg.org/ac/terms/widthFrac> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <http://rs.tdwg.org/ac/terms/> .
<http://rs.tdwg.org/ac/terms/widthFrac> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Fractional Width"@en .
<http://rs.tdwg.org/ac/terms/widthFrac> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The width of the bounding rectangle, expressed as a decimal fraction of the width of the media item."@en .
<http://rs.tdwg.org/ac/terms/widthFrac> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Fractional Width"@en .
<http://rs.tdwg.org/ac/terms/widthFrac> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "The sum of a valid value plus ac:xFrac MUST be greater than zero and less than or equal to one. The precision of this value SHOULD be great enough that when ac:widthFrac and ac:xFrac are used with the exif:PixelXDimension of the Best Quality variant of the Service Access point to calculate the lower right corner of the rectangle, rounding to the nearest integer results in the same horizontal pixel originally used to define the point. This term MUST NOT be used with ac:radius to define a region of interest."@en .
<http://rs.tdwg.org/ac/terms/xFrac.rdf> <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator> "Biodiversity Information Standards (TDWG)" .
<http://rs.tdwg.org/ac/terms/xFrac.rdf> <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/format> "application/rdf+xml" .
<http://rs.tdwg.org/ac/terms/xFrac.rdf> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/modified> "2021-10-07T13:17:47-05:00"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> .
<http://rs.tdwg.org/ac/terms/xFrac.rdf> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/references> <http://rs.tdwg.org/ac/terms/xFrac> .
<http://rs.tdwg.org/ac/terms/xFrac.rdf> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/document> .
<http://rs.tdwg.org/ac/terms/xFrac> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "2021-10-05"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
<http://rs.tdwg.org/ac/terms/xFrac> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "This point can serve as the horizontal position of the upper left corner of a bounding rectangle, or as the center of a circle."@en .
<http://rs.tdwg.org/ac/terms/xFrac> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/hasVersion> <http://rs.tdwg.org/ac/terms/version/xFrac-2021-10-05> .
<http://rs.tdwg.org/ac/terms/xFrac> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/isPartOf> <http://rs.tdwg.org/ac/terms/> .
<http://rs.tdwg.org/ac/terms/xFrac> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/modified> "2021-10-05"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
<http://rs.tdwg.org/ac/terms/xFrac> <http://rs.tdwg.org/dwc/terms/attributes/organizedInClass> <http://rs.tdwg.org/ac/terms/RegionOfInterest> .
<http://rs.tdwg.org/ac/terms/xFrac> <http://rs.tdwg.org/dwc/terms/attributes/repeatable> "No" .
<http://rs.tdwg.org/ac/terms/xFrac> <http://rs.tdwg.org/dwc/terms/attributes/required> "No" .
<http://rs.tdwg.org/ac/terms/xFrac> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#Property> .
<http://rs.tdwg.org/ac/terms/xFrac> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The horizontal position of a reference point, measured from the left side of the media item and expressed as a decimal fraction of the width of the media item."@en .
<http://rs.tdwg.org/ac/terms/xFrac> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <http://rs.tdwg.org/ac/terms/> .
<http://rs.tdwg.org/ac/terms/xFrac> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Fractional X"@en .
<http://rs.tdwg.org/ac/terms/xFrac> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The horizontal position of a reference point, measured from the left side of the media item and expressed as a decimal fraction of the width of the media item."@en .
<http://rs.tdwg.org/ac/terms/xFrac> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Fractional X"@en .
<http://rs.tdwg.org/ac/terms/xFrac> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "A valid value MUST be greater than or equal to zero and less than or equal to one. The precision of this value SHOULD be great enough that when the ac:xFrac value is multiplied by the exif:PixelXDimension of the Best Quality variant of the Service Access point, rounding to the nearest integer results in the same horizontal pixel location originally used to define the point."@en .
<http://rs.tdwg.org/ac/terms/yFrac.rdf> <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator> "Biodiversity Information Standards (TDWG)" .
<http://rs.tdwg.org/ac/terms/yFrac.rdf> <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/format> "application/rdf+xml" .
<http://rs.tdwg.org/ac/terms/yFrac.rdf> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/modified> "2021-10-07T13:17:47-05:00"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> .
<http://rs.tdwg.org/ac/terms/yFrac.rdf> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/references> <http://rs.tdwg.org/ac/terms/yFrac> .
<http://rs.tdwg.org/ac/terms/yFrac.rdf> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/document> .
<http://rs.tdwg.org/ac/terms/yFrac> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "2021-10-05"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
<http://rs.tdwg.org/ac/terms/yFrac> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "This point can serve as the vertical position of the upper left corner of a bounding rectangle, or as the center of a circle."@en .
<http://rs.tdwg.org/ac/terms/yFrac> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/hasVersion> <http://rs.tdwg.org/ac/terms/version/yFrac-2021-10-05> .
<http://rs.tdwg.org/ac/terms/yFrac> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/isPartOf> <http://rs.tdwg.org/ac/terms/> .
<http://rs.tdwg.org/ac/terms/yFrac> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/modified> "2021-10-05"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
<http://rs.tdwg.org/ac/terms/yFrac> <http://rs.tdwg.org/dwc/terms/attributes/organizedInClass> <http://rs.tdwg.org/ac/terms/RegionOfInterest> .
<http://rs.tdwg.org/ac/terms/yFrac> <http://rs.tdwg.org/dwc/terms/attributes/repeatable> "No" .
<http://rs.tdwg.org/ac/terms/yFrac> <http://rs.tdwg.org/dwc/terms/attributes/required> "No" .
<http://rs.tdwg.org/ac/terms/yFrac> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#Property> .
<http://rs.tdwg.org/ac/terms/yFrac> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The vertical position of a reference point, measured from the top of the media item and expressed as a decimal fraction of the height of the media item."@en .
<http://rs.tdwg.org/ac/terms/yFrac> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <http://rs.tdwg.org/ac/terms/> .
<http://rs.tdwg.org/ac/terms/yFrac> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Fractional Y"@en .
<http://rs.tdwg.org/ac/terms/yFrac> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The vertical position of a reference point, measured from the top of the media item and expressed as a decimal fraction of the height of the media item."@en .
<http://rs.tdwg.org/ac/terms/yFrac> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Fractional Y"@en .
<http://rs.tdwg.org/ac/terms/yFrac> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "A valid value MUST be greater than or equal to zero and less than or equal to one. The precision of this value SHOULD be great enough that when the ac:yFrac value is multiplied by the exif:PixelYDimension of the Best Quality variant of the Service Access point, rounding to the nearest integer results in the same vertical pixel originally used to define the point."@en .
